One of the five वम्शवीरस्.
४२: Ib. III. ७२. 1.
After his great Decease Arjuna felt himself powerless even against आभिरस्;
४३: Vi. V. ३८. ४७-51;

--a son of Vipracitti. Lord of the Asuras, hostile to Indra;
1: Vi. I. २१. ११.
a resident of the first talam or atala;
2: वा. ५०. १५; ९८. ८१.
a nephew of हिरण्यकशिपु; married सुप्रभा, the daughter of स्वर्भानु;
3: भा.

. २७.
followed वृत्र against Indra;
4: भा. VI. १०. १९-31; Br. II. २०. १६.
took part in the देवासुर war between Bali and Indra; fought with अपराजित; heard of Bali's and Jambha's fall and fought with Indra; resisted with success Vajra on account of the fact that he could not be killed either by a dry or wet thing; Indra who came to know of this by a voice in the air used फेन (foam) and killed him to the satisfaction of all gods;
5: भा.

; VIII. १०. २० to the end; ११. १९, २३, २९-40; M. २२. ६१.
